    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.files\n\n### Description\n\nHi echasnovski! As of now, in a mini.files buffer, it is possible to edit the filetype icons as well and remove them by pressing backspace when in insert mode in the mini.files buffer. Is it possible to enable statuscolumn with options \"auto:1\" so that it only comes up when mini.icons is enabled in mini.files buffers, link statuscolumn bg to mini.files buffer bg, and put all the filetype icons in statuscolumn in order to prevent them from being removed or edited.",
