        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nI am afraid, this is not really possible. The main reason is that prefix (which can be not only 'mini.icons' icons) should also react on text manipulation during editing. Otherwise deleting/moving lines in explorer will make prefixes in statuscolumn out of date. There are, of course, methods to adjust that, but they are far more complex than just having it be part of the text.\n\nBesides, removing only prefix from the text will not solve the problem of \"accidental `<BS>` removes something that should not be removed\". There *needs* to be [an identifier (concealed)](https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-files.html#minifiles-manipulation-howdoesitwork) along with the text to track file system manipulation. So even if there is no icons/prefix, the `<BS>` will delete part of the concealed identifier.",
            "created_at": "2025-10-27T16:01:45Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/2093#issuecomment-3452075610",
